    "introduction": "Unilever develops and markets everyday consumer products across beauty and wellbeing, personal care, home care and foods. Brands such as Dove, Persil, Hellmann's and Knorr reach consumers through supermarkets, smaller retailers, online channels and food-service distributors. The company combines product formulation, brand marketing, manufacturing and distribution, earning revenue from products that households buy repeatedly. Its international reach includes both established consumer markets and economies where spending patterns are still developing. Brand recognition and retail availability support demand, but success also depends on product innovation, competitive pricing and managing ingredient, packaging and transport costs across a complex global supply chain.",
